{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\ninput = lambda: sys.stdin.readline().rstrip()\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1000000)\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    m = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    L = n * (n - 1) + 1\n\n    def rec(i, dp_prev, dp1_prev):\n        if i > n:\n            return sum(dp1_prev[m + 1:]) % mod\n        start = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        end = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) // 2\n        dp_cur = [0] * L\n        dp1_cur = [0] * L\n        for x in range(start, end + 1):\n            dp1_cur[x] = dp1_prev[x] * i % mod\n        for x in range(start, end + 1):\n            v = dp_prev[x]\n            if v:\n                for d in range(-i + 1, i):\n                    dp_cur[x + d] = (dp_cur[x + d] + v * (i - abs(d))) % mod\n                for d in range(1, i):\n                    dp1_cur[x - d] = (dp1_cur[x - d] + v * (i - d)) % mod\n        return rec(i + 1, dp_cur, dp1_cur)\n\n    init_dp = [0] * L\n    init_dp[m] = 1\n    init_dp1 = [0] * L\n    return rec(2, init_dp, init_dp1)\n\nprint(solve())\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    long long m = n * (n - 1) / 2;\n    long long L = n * (n - 1) + 1;\n\n    vector<long long> dp(L, 0);\n    vector<long long> dp1(L, 0);\n    dp[m] = 1;\n\n    for (long long i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long start = m - (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n        long long end = m + (i - 1) * (i - 2) / 2;\n\n        vector<long long> dp_cur(L, 0);\n        vector<long long> dp1_cur(L, 0);\n\n        // First loop: dp1_cur[x] = dp1[x] * i % mod\n        for (long long x = start; x <= end; ++x) {\n            dp1_cur[x] = (dp1[x] * i) % mod;\n        }\n\n        // Second loop: contributions from dp\n        for (long long x = start; x <= end; ++x) {\n            long long v = dp[x];\n            if (v != 0) {\n                // d from -i+1 to i-1\n                for (long long d = -i + 1; d < i; ++d) {\n                    long long idx = x + d;\n                    if (idx >= 0 && idx < L) {\n                        dp_cur[idx] = (dp_cur[idx] + v * (i - abs(d))) % mod;\n                    }\n                }\n                // d from 1 to i-1\n                for (long long d = 1; d < i; ++d) {\n                    long long idx = x - d;\n                    if (idx >= 0 && idx < L) {\n                        dp1_cur[idx] = (dp1_cur[idx] + v * (i - d)) % mod;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        dp = move(dp_cur);\n        dp1 = move(dp1_cur);\n    }\n\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for (long long x = m + 1; x < L; ++x) {\n        ans = (ans + dp1[x]) % mod;\n    }\n    cout << ans << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.003899234114214778, -3.933898824470816e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.000290470838